hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16827","Abd Allah narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna narrated to me, he said: Ma'di ibn Sulayman narrated to us, he said: Shu'ayth ibn Mutayr narrated to us from his father Mutayr, and Mutayr was present confirming his statement, he said: How did I tell you? He said: O my father, you told me that Dhu al-Yadayn met you at Dhi Khushub and informed you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them one of the two afternoon prayers, and it was Asr, and he prayed two rak'as, and the hasty people went out saying: Has the prayer been shortened? And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood, and Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, followed him, and they were close behind, and Dhu al-Yadayn caught up with him and said: O Messenger of Allah, has the prayer been shortened, has the prayer been shortened, or did you forget? And he said: It has neither been shortened nor did I forget. Then he turned to Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, and said: What is Dhu al-Yadayn saying? And they said: He spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, and the people came back, and he prayed two rak'as, then he gave the salutation, then he prostrated the two prostrations of forgetfulness. Abu Sulayman said: I narrated it for six or seven years, then he gave the salutation, and I was uncertain about it, though it is the more preserved in my memory."
"16828","Abd Allah narrated to us, Nasr ibn Ali narrated to me, he said: Ma'di ibn Sulayman informed me, he said: I came to Mutayr to ask him about the hadith of Dhu al-Yadayn, and I came to him and asked him, and he was an old man who could not get the hadith out due to old age, and his son Shu'ayth said: Yes, O my father, you narrated to me that Dhu al-Yadayn met you at Dhi Khashab and narrated to you that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed with them one of the two afternoon prayers, and it was Asr, two rak'as, then he gave the salutation, and the hasty people went out and said: Has the prayer been shortened? And among the people were Abu Bakr and Umar, and Dhu al-Yadayn said: Has the prayer been shortened or did you forget? He said: The prayer has neither been shortened nor did I forget. Then he turned to Abu Bakr and Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, and said: What is Dhu al-Yadayn saying? And they said: He spoke the truth, O Messenger of Allah. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned, and the people came back, and he prayed with them two rak'as, then he gave the salutation, then he prostrated with them the two prostrations of forgetfulness."
"16829","Abd Allah narrated to us, Abu Ma'mar narrated to me from Ibn Abi Hazim, he said: A man came to Ali ibn Husayn and said: What was the standing of Abu Bakr and Umar with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? And he said: Their standing right now."
